.SH "NAME"
nvme-ocp-persistent-event-log \- Send NVMe persistent event log page request, returns result and log additional OCP\-specific data
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.nf
\fInvme\fR [<global\-options>] \fIocp persistent\-event\-log\fR <device>
                        [\-\-action=<action> | \-a <action>]
                        [\-\-log\-len=<log\-len> | \-l <log\-len>]
                        [\-\-raw\-binary | \-b]
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
Retrieves the NVMe persistent event log page from an NVMe device and provides the returned structure\&.
.sp
The <device> parameter is mandatory and may be either the NVMe character device (ex: /dev/nvme0), or a namespace block device (ex: /dev/nvme0n1)\&.
.sp
On success, the returned persistent event log structure may be returned in one of several ways depending on the option flags; the structure may parsed by the program and printed in a readable format or the raw buffer may be printed to stdout for another program to parse\&.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
\-a <action>, \-\-action=<action>
.RS 4
The action the controller takes with the reporting context of the log\&. 0 (Read Log Data) reads the log of an established context\&. 1 (Establish Context and Read Log Data) establishes a context, and fails if one is established\&. 2 (Release Context) releases the context\&. 3 (Establish Context and Read 512 Bytes of Header) establishes a context unless one is established, and reads only the log header\&. Defaults to 3\&. A context stays established until it is released with action 2\&. Action 3 requires ECRH support\&. For more details see the NVM Express Base Specification, Revision 2\&.1, section 5\&.1\&.12\&.1\&.14 Persistent Event (Log Page Identifier 0Dh)\&.
.RE
.PP
\-l <log\-len>, \-\-log\-len=<log\-len>
.RS 4
The number of bytes of the log to read\&. Without it, or with 0, action 0 reads the Total Log Length (TLL) of the log, and action 1 only establishes the context\&. Actions 2 and 3 ignore it\&.
.RE
.PP
\-b, \-\-raw\-binary
.RS 4
Print the raw persistent event log buffer to stdout\&.
.RE
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.sp
The following options are defined at the top\-level nvme command and are available to this subcommand:
.PP
\-\-dry\-run
.RS 4
Print the command that would be executed, but do not actually execute it\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-no\-ioctl\-probing
.RS 4
Disable probing for 64\-bit IOCTL support\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-no\-retries
.RS 4
Disable retry logic on transient errors\&.
.RE
.PP
\-o <fmt>, \-\-output\-format=<fmt>
.RS 4
Set the reporting format to
\fInormal\fR,
\fItabular, \*(Aqjson\fR, or
\fIbinary\fR\&. Only one output format may be used at a time\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-output\-format\-version=<version>
.RS 4
Select the output format version\&. Version
\fI1\fR
uses the original field naming, while version
\fI2\fR
(default) provides more consistent and script\-friendly field names\&. Other versions are rejected\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-quiet
.RS 4
Suppress informational messages\&. Errors are still reported, and \-\-quiet cancels any \-\-verbose for the library log level\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-set\-options=<key=value>[,<key=value>\&...]
.RS 4
Set libnvme library options for this invocation\&. Supported keys are
\fIforce\-4k\fR,
\fImi\-probe\-enabled\fR,
\fItest\-base\-dir\fR
and
\fItest\-sysfs\-dir\fR\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-timeout=<ms>
.RS 4
Set the timeout for the command in milliseconds\&.
\fIinfinite\fR
or
\fI\-1\fR
waits without a time limit (0xffffffff)\&.
.RE
.PP
\-v, \-\-verbose
.RS 4
Increase the level of detail in the output\&. May be specified multiple times to further increase verbosity\&.
.RE
.sp
These options can also be set as machine\-wide defaults in nvme\-cli\&.conf(5)\&. A command\-line flag always overrides the file\&.
